  "query_preview": "..\n\nA retrograding surface trough will produce areas of fog across\nnortheast Montana through this morning. The fog will originate\nnear Plentywood and spread across regions north of the Missouri \nRiver as the morning progresses. Additional fog may be present in \nregions surrounding the Yellowstone Valley. Visibilities as low as\n1/4 mile are possible northeast of Wolf Point.\n\nAn upper-level ridge over Montana will result in dry conditions\nand temperatures 10 to 15 degrees above seasonal averages \npersisting though the weekend.\n\nModel ensembles begin to exhibit significant discrepancies around\nTuesday afternoon. The ECMWF indicates a trough will begin to dig\nover the Rockies around this time, but it is possible the ridge \nwill persist longer than this.\n\nFORECAST CONFIDENCE & DEVIATIONS:\n\n- Added fog in the northeast regions of Montana. No further\n  deviations from the NBM were made. \n \n- Confidence in fog placement and visibilities this morning is\n  moderate (70%).\n\n- Confidence in fair conditions persisting through Monday is high\n  (90%).\n\n\nDON",
